From: Long Way Home <noreply@long-way-home.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] single player: menus that do not pause the game

The SP bridge freezes the simulation whenever a menu or the console is up. A ship's console is
operated while the ship carries on around the operator, so a menu may now declare itself live by
setting ui_liveMenu while it is open; the simulation then keeps running behind it. The flag is
cleared by the engine as soon as no menu is open, so it cannot leak to the next menu (ESC,
save/load), which pause exactly as before. The console always pauses.

A live menu must also not be "fullscreen" in the UI's sense: a fullscreen menu stops the game
being drawn, and in this bridge the game's frame is driven from its draw.
---
diff --git a/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/sp/sp_integration.c b/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/sp/sp_integration.c
--- a/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/sp/sp_integration.c
+++ b/EFAndroid-SP/app/jni/sp/sp_integration.c
@@ -430,7 +430,14 @@
 // mission. Mirroring retail SV_Frame (which skips the sim while sv_paused/cl_paused) keeps the world
 // frozen behind the FMV; the cgame still re-draws that frozen frame so the overlay sits on top.
 int SP_MenuPaused(void){
-    if ( Key_GetCatcher() & ( KEYCATCH_UI | KEYCATCH_CONSOLE ) ) return 1;
+    // Long Way Home: a "live" screen -- a ship console the player operates while the ship carries on
+    // around them -- sets ui_liveMenu while it is up, and the simulation is not paused for it. The
+    // flag is cleared here as soon as no menu is open, so it can never leak to the next menu (ESC,
+    // save/load), which pause as they always have. The console always pauses.
+    if ( Key_GetCatcher() & KEYCATCH_CONSOLE ) return 1;
+    if ( !( Key_GetCatcher() & KEYCATCH_UI ) ) {
+        if ( Cvar_VariableIntegerValue( "ui_liveMenu" ) ) Cvar_Set( "ui_liveMenu", "0" );
+    } else if ( !Cvar_VariableIntegerValue( "ui_liveMenu" ) ) return 1;
     if ( Cvar_VariableIntegerValue( "cl_paused" ) ) return 1;
     return 0;
 }
